re an M.S. thesis, which is not required for the degree, may take up to 8 units of EARTHSYS 299 with their master's advisor and must complete 1 unit of EARTHSYS 299A.","notes":"M.S. Thesis Resources\nApplication Process and Deadlines\nM.S. Thesis Guidelines","t":"courses","items":[["EARTHSYS 299"],["EARTHSYS 299A"]],"optional":true,"mode":"all"},{"id":"Za9a0Tid","t":"courses","name":"Remaining coursework at the 100 level or above","mode":"any","pool":{"subjects":[],"anySubject":true,"minNumber":100},"notes":"The Master of Science degree in Earth Systems allows specialization through graduate-level coursework.\nThe following are required of all M.S. students:\n\n• A minimum of 45 units of coursework and/or research credit (upon approval).\n\n• At least 34 units of the student’s coursework for the master’s program must be at the 200-level or above. All remaining coursework must be at the 100-level or above.\n\n• Up to nine units of research (Earthsys 297 and/or Earthsys 250) may be completed with their Master’s Advisor. This will enrich building mastery in the field through regular communication with their Master's Advisor.\n\n• Students may use 8 units of Earthsys 323: Stanford at Sea towards the required 45 units. Please note- Although the entire 16 unit course must be in your graduate career, only 8 units will be applied towards the required 45 units.","reviewed":true},{"id":"ov-easys-gpa","t":"text","name":"Overall GPA of at least 3.4","manual":"gpa","reviewed":true}],"units":45}],"unitsMin":45,"gpa":"A minimum overall GPA of 3.4 must be maintained.","grading":"All courses for the master’s program must be taken for a letter grade; courses not taken for a letter grade must be approved by the master’s advisor and Director of Earth Systems.","policies":"Prerequisite courses may not be counted toward the 45 required MS units.\nCompletion of prerequisite courses is not required prior to applying to the coterm program; however, all prerequisite courses must be completed prior to graduation.\nStudents may petition to have alternative courses satisfy pre-requisite courses listed in the \"Pre-requisite Coursework\" section below.","transferPolicy":"Pre-requisite courses may be fulfilled through approved AP credit, Stanford placement tests, or transfer credit, where applicable. Students can submit a petition for such credit to be counted.\nTransfer courses from other institutions may not be counted toward the required 45 units.","reviewed":"2026-10-23","reviewNotes":"Every course must be letter graded. You complete one set of prerequisites, which do not count toward the 45 units, and then 45 units of program coursework: the Master's Seminar and at least 34 units at the 200 level or above, with the rest at the 100 level or above. At most 9 units of research (EARTHSYS 297 and 250), 8 units of Stanford at Sea (EARTHSYS 323) and 8 units of thesis (EARTHSYS 299) count. Your advisor checks the 3.4 GPA and any course approved without a letter grade.","letterGrade":true,"totals":[{"label":"Research units (EARTHSYS 297, EARTHSYS 250)","maxUnits":9,"codes":["EARTHSYS 297","EARTHSYS 250"],"inRules":true},{"label":"EARTHSYS 323 (Stanford at Sea)","maxUnits":8,"codes":["EARTHSYS 323"],"inRules":true},{"label":"EARTHSYS 299 (M.S. thesis)","maxUnits":8,"codes":["EARTHSYS 299"],"inRules":true}]}